1️⃣ Benefits of Using API Gateway
a) Single Entry Point

Clients don’t need to know the addresses of multiple services.
Example:

GET https://api.bank.com/accounts
GET https://api.bank.com/transactions

Instead of:

GET https://userservice.local/api/users
GET https://orderservice.local/api/orders
GET https://paymentservice.local/api/payments
b) Centralized Security

The gateway can handle:

Authentication (JWT, OAuth2)

Authorization (role-based access)

Unauthorized requests are blocked at the gateway, before hitting any microservice.

c) Rate Limiting

The gateway can restrict the number of requests per client or IP.

Example:

Max 100 requests per minute per user

Prevents API abuse and DDoS attacks.

d) Load Balancing

The gateway distributes requests across multiple service instances:

API Gateway
   ↓
User Service Instance 1
User Service Instance 2
User Service Instance 3

Improves availability and scalability.

e) Request/Response Transformation

The gateway can:

Add/remove headers

Transform request or response formats

Aggregate responses from multiple services

Example: Combine user and order info in one response.

f) Logging & Monitoring

The gateway centralizes logs and metrics:

API usage

Errors

Performance metrics

Helps in debugging, auditing, and security monitoring.

